==English==

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|frm|irrégularité}}, from {{der|en|ML.|irregularitas}}.

Morphologically {{suffix|en|irregular|ity|nocat=1}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP|nMmmm}} {{IPA|en|/ɪˌɹɛ.ɡjʊˈlæ.ɹɪ.ti/}}
* {{a|GA|Mmmm}} {{IPA|en|/ɪˌɹɛ.ɡjəˈlɛɹ.ɪ.ti/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-irregularity.wav|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|countable}} An instance of being [[irregular]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The state or condition of being irregular, or the extent to which something is irregular.
# {{lb|en|countable}} An [[object]] or [[event]] that is not [[regular]] or [[ordinary]].
#: {{ux|en|an '''irregularity''' of surface}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} A [[violation]] of rules.
#: {{ux|en|An investigation of the '''irregularities''' in the company's accounts uncovered a large-scale fraud.}}
# {{lb|en|euphemism}} Irregular bowel movement (e.g. [[diarrhea]] or [[constipation]]).
#* {{quote-book|en|author=James Dallas Jardine; Indu Vaid|title=Alternative Therapies|publisher=Health Harmony|year=2000|isbn=8170218551|page=246|passage=Consuming copious amounts of vegetables, fruit, milk, and an abundance of water effectively treats '''irregularity'''. Establishing regular eating, bowel movement, and exercise habits are helpful too.}}

